  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BUILDING A ROBUST DATA FOUNDATION FOR UKRAINE&apos;S DISPLACEMENT STRATEGY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the contribution from the Government of Canada, IOM proposes to strengthen its assessment and data-generation capacities, coordination mechanisms, and support to evidence-based governance. The aim is to enable government counterparts, humanitarian and recovery actors, and other stakeholders across all sectors of the Ukraine response to rapidly identify the needs, movements, and intentions of affected populations. This will help address emerging challenges and improve the coherence and effectiveness of humanitarian and recovery interventions for war-affected communities in Ukraine through:  Timely data generation, providing credible and operationally relevant information on population presence, mobility, and needs; Data coordination, facilitating and promoting the use of data across humanitarian and recovery actors in Ukraine; and Evidence-based governance, delivering technical assistance and expertise to government institutions and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
